\tag{discrete}
\taxon{Example}

\import{discrete-macros}

\p{#{g} is not [not injective](00A3), since #{\diamond \neq \square} but #{g(\diamond) =
g(\square) = 6}. We could easily make a different function with the same domain and codomain which is injective. For example, the function which is the same as #{g} on #{\triangle} and #{\square} but sends #{\diamond} to #{349}.}

